        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: NOAA Weather Radio\n- Places: North Georgia mountains, Blue Ridge, Georgia, Young Harris, Brasstown Bald\n- Products: KXI75, KXI22\n\nFacts:\n- NOAA Weather Radio station KXI75 is an older station that serves about half of the north Georgia mountains.\n- KXI75 broadcasts at 300 watts on 162.475 MHz from a location near Blue Ridge, Georgia.\n- KXI75 is now simulcast on newer station KXI22.\n- KXI22 is located atop Brasstown Bald near Young Harris, which is the highest point in the U.S. state of Georgia.",
